<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego Columbus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1479–<a href="/years/1526">1526</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Diego Colón</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diego <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a> was the eldest son of Christopher Columbus and governor of the Indies at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> from 1509. Pursuing his father's hereditary claims against the Spanish crown, he won recognition as admiral and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-esquivel">Juan de Esquivel</a> to settle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> in 1509 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez">Diego Velázquez</a> to conquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> in 1511. He was recalled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1523 and died in 1526.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-columbus.jpg" alt="Diego Columbus" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diego_Colon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
